{
  "name": "v12-weight-floor-and-dust",
  "description": "A supply of 10,000,000 over a 22 s window makes the weight floor 10,000,000 / 10^6 x 22 = 220. Epoch 1 (blocks 100-110): carol (11 x 22 = 242) weighs; erin weighs (5 x 6 + 15 x 16 = 270: 10 more from block 103); ivan holds 100 for blocks 100-103 (800) and then passes it through four fresh addresses, one block each (100 x 2 = 200 each: none weighs), to a fifth that keeps it (600); frank gets 10 in block 105 and drops to 9 in block 107 (112: no weight); gina (1) and nine dust holders (5 each) never weigh. 100 wei of income gives only alice and bob a share, so carol, erin, ivan and the fifth address weigh, count in W, and are not listed; the file lists only alice and bob and their balances, and commits to every balance. Epoch 2 (blocks 111-120, 20 s) opens at the complete state: a dust holder sends its 5 to dave (a replay from the listed balances alone would go below zero); erin sells to hank in block 115 (120: no weight) and hank holds 15 from then (180); alice burns 1,000,000, so the supply after T is 9,000,000 and the floor 9 x 20 = 180, which frank (9 x 20) and hank meet exactly. 100,000,000 more wei gives the small holders a share.",
  "covers": [
    "weight floor = supply after T / 10^6 x window seconds",
    "a weight at the floor counts, one below it does not",
    "one amount passed through fresh addresses block by block weighs nothing",
    "a holder who buys or sells inside the window",
    "weight without a share is not listed",
    "dust carried in the complete state, not in the file",
    "dust sent in a later epoch",
    "a burn moves the floor"
  ],
